From 7f4d44b7a875183b5b63e6b346a7eac15b938d3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:14:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Harden Windows Hello, 1Password and drop handling from review

The Windows Hello broker discards replies to earlier requests, so an interrupted sudo no longer leaves every later one reading the previous answer. It refuses terminals that belong to a remote login session, and after a denial it uses the password on that terminal for 30 seconds so a mistyped password does not bring the prompt back. The 1Password agent reads the process start time before and after its checks and rejects a 1Password started with ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, LD_PRELOAD or NODE_OPTIONS; its unit no longer waits on the virtio port symlink, which could make it skip itself at boot. The drop receiver sends its ticket ID with drop-drag and asks only once Hyprland shows the drag source. Display sync records a reload mode only when one display is connected, and its reload watcher stops after repeated quick disconnects. Revision 39 delivers these to existing guests.
